    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   111→  },\n   112→  {\n   113→    \"title\": \"Latent Phase-Shift Rollback: Inference-Time Error Correction via Residual Stream Monitoring and KV-Cache Steering\",\n   114→    \"description\": \"Novel approach for inference-time error correction in LLMs through residual stream monitoring and KV-cache steering. Under review. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   115→    \"author\": \"Manan Gupta, Dhruv Kumar\",\n   116→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   117→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18567\",\n   118→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   119→    \"topics\": [\"LLMs\", \"error correction\", \"inference\", \"KV-cache\"],\n   120→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"Train Separately, Merge Together: Modular Post-Training with Mixture-of-Experts\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"Research on modular post-training with mixture-of-experts approaches. Proposes training separate modules and merging them. 9 content pages, 23 pages overall. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"Jacob Morrison, Sanjay Adhikesaven, Akshita Bhagia, Matei Zaharia, Noah A. Smith, Sewon Min\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18473\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\"MoE\", \"modular training\", \"post-training\", \"LLMs\"],\n   130→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"title\": \"Knowing When to Quit: A Principled Framework for Dynamic Abstention in LLM Reasoning\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"Framework for dynamic abstention in LLM reasoning - knowing when the model should refrain from answering. Addresses reliability and calibration issues in LLM outputs. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   135→    \"author\": \"Hen Davidov, Nachshon Cohen, Oren Kalinsky, Yaron Fairstein, Guy Kushilevitz, Ram Yazdi, Patrick Rebeschini\",\n   136→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18419\",\n   138→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   139→    \"topics\": [\"LLMs\", \"reasoning\", \"abstention\", \"calibration\", \"reliability\"],\n   140→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   141→  },\n   142→  {\n   143→    \"title\": \"MathNet: a Global Multimodal Benchmark for Mathematical Reasoning and Retrieval\",\n   144→    \"description\": \"New benchmark for mathematical reasoning and retrieval using multimodal approaches. ICLR 2026 paper with website. Addresses mathematical reasoning capabilities in AI systems. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   145→    \"author\": \"Shaden Alshammari, Kevin Wen, Abrar Zainal, Mark Hamilton, Navid Safaei, Sultan Albarakati, William T. Freeman, Antonio Torralba\",\n   146→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   147→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18584\",\n   148→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   149→    \"topics\": [\"math\", \"reasoning\", \"multimodal\", \"benchmark\", \"ICLR 2026\"],\n   150→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   151→  },\n   152→  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"Agentic Forecasting using Sequential Bayesian Updating of Linguistic Beliefs\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"Paper on agentic forecasting approaches using sequential Bayesian updating of linguistic beliefs. Addresses how AI agents can update beliefs and make forecasts. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"Kevin Murphy\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18576\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"forecasting\", \"Bayesian\", \"agentic AI\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"ClawEnvKit: Automatic Environment Generation for Claw-Like Agents\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Framework for automatic environment generation for Claw-like agents (similar to OpenClaw). Addresses agent testing and environment synthesis. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Xirui Li, Ming Li, Derry Xu, Wei-Lin Chiang, Ion Stoica, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Tianyi Zhou\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18543\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"OpenClaw\", \"environment generation\", \"testing\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"LLM Safety From Within: Detecting Harmful Content with Internal Representations\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Research on detecting harmful content using LLM internal representations rather than external filters. 17 pages, 10 figures, 6 tables. Addresses AI safety through internal monitoring. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"Difan Jiao, Yilun Liu, Ye Yuan, Zhenwei Tang, Linfeng Du, Haolun Wu, Ashton Anderson\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18519\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"AI safety\", \"LLMs\", \"harmful content\", \"internal representations\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"WorldDB: A Vector Graph-of-Worlds Memory Engine with Ontology-Aware Write-Time Reconciliation\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"Novel memory engine approach using vector graph-of-worlds with ontology-aware reconciliation during writes. Addresses persistent memory and knowledge representation for AI agents. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"Harish Santhanalakshmi Ganesan\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18478\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"memory\", \"knowledge graphs\", \"agents\", \"vectors\", \"ontology\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"Using large language models for embodied planning introduces systematic safety risks\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Research identifying systematic safety risks when using LLMs for embodied planning in robotics. Important safety considerations for AI agents in physical environments. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"Tao Zhang, Kaixian Qu, Zhibin Li, Jiajun Wu, Marco Hutter, Manling Li, Fan Shi\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18463\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"safety\", \"robotics\", \"embodied AI\", \"planning\", \"LLMs\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Training and Agentic Inference Strategies for LLM-based Manim Animation Generation\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"Research on training and inference strategies for using LLMs to generate Manim animations. Addresses agentic approaches to animation and video generation. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"Ravidu Suien Rammuni Silva, Ahmad Lotfi, Isibor Kennedy Ihianle, Golnaz Shahtahmassebi, Jordan J. Bird\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18364\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"LLMs\", \"animation\", \"manim\", \"agentic inference\", \"generation\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"LeGo-Code: Can Modular Curriculum Learning Advance Complex Code Generation? Insights from Text-to-SQL\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"Research on whether modular curriculum learning can advance complex code generation, using Text-to-SQL as a test case. 7 pages, 3 figures, 4 tables. Published 2026-04-21.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"Salmane Chafik, Saad Ezzini, Ismail Berrada\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18254\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"code generation\", \"SQL\", \"curriculum learning\", \"modular learning\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   221→  },\n   222→  {\n   223→    \"title\": \"Release: llm-openrouter 0.6\",\n   224→    \"description\": \"Released llm-openrouter 0.6 with a new `llm openrouter refresh` command for refreshing the list of available models without waiting for cache to expire. Simon added this feature to try Kimi 2.6 on OpenRouter as soon as it became available. Generated an animated pelican on a bicycle using the model.\",\n   225→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   226→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   227→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/llm-openrouter-0-6/\",\n   228→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n   229→    \"topics\": [\"openrouter\", \"LLM\", \"LLM release\", \"pelican-riding-a-bicycle\", \"kimi\", \"AI in China\", \"LLMs\", \"AI\", \"Generative AI\"],\n   230→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   231→  },\n   232→  {\n   233→    \"title\": \"TIL: SQL functions in Google Sheets to fetch data from Datasette\",\n   234→    \"description\": \"Documented patterns for fetching data from a Datasette instance directly into Google Sheets using three methods: the `importdata()` function, a named function that wraps it, or a Google Apps Script for API token authentication in HTTP headers.\",\n   235→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   236→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   237→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/sheets-datasette/\",\n   238→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n   239→    \"topics\": [\"spreadsheets\", \"datasette\", \"google\"],\n   240→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   241→  },\n   242→  {\n   243→    \"title\": \"Claude Token Counter with model comparisons\",\n   244→    \"description\": \"Upgraded Claude Token Counter tool to add ability to run the same count against different models for comparison. Claude Opus 4.7 is the first model to change the tokenizer. Found that Opus 4.7's tokenizer uses 1.46x the tokens of Opus 4.6 for the system prompt, and 3.01x for high-resolution images due to improved resolution support (up to 2,576 pixels on long edge, ~3.75 megapixels).\",\n   245→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   246→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   247→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/claude-token-counter/\",\n   248→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n   249→    \"topics\": [\"AI\", \"Generative AI\", \"LLMs\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"LLM pricing\", \"tokenization\"],\n   250→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   251→  },\n   252→  {\n   253→    \"title\": \"Headless everything for personal AI\",\n   254→    \"description\": \"Discussion about the trend toward headless services becoming more common for personal AI usage. Matt Webb argues headless services are better for personal AIs than GUI-based interfaces. Salesforce launched Salesforce Headless 360 exposing their platform as APIs, MCP, & CLI. Brandur Leach predicts APIs are making a comeback as a major vector for AI agent integration.\",\n   255→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison, Matt Webb, Marc Benioff, Brandur Leach\",\n   256→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   257→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/19/headless/\",\n   258→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-19\",\n   259→    \"topics\": [\"APIs\", \"definitions\", \"matt-webb\", \"salesforce\", \"saas\", \"AI\", \"brandur-leach\"],\n   260→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   261→  },\n   262→  {\n   263→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-Max-Preview: Smarter, Sharper, Still Evolving\",\n   264→    \"description\": \"Following the release of Qwen3.6-Plus, Alibaba released an early preview of Qwen3.6-Max-Preview. Compared to Qwen3.6-Plus, this preview brings stronger world knowledge and instruction following, along with significant agentic coding improvements across a wide range of benchmarks. As a preview, the model is still under active development.\",\n   265→    \"author\": \"Qwen Team (Alibaba)\",\n   266→    \"source\": \"Platform\",\n   267→    \"url\": \"https://qwen.ai\",\n   268→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n   269→    \"topics\": [\"qwen\", \"AI\", \"LLMs\", \"agentic coding\", \"LLM release\"],\n   270→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   271→  },\n   272→  {\n   273→    \"title\": \"Changes in the system prompt between Claude Opus 4.6 and 4.7\",\n   274→    \"description\": \"Anthropic published the system prompts for their user-facing chat systems. Simon analyzed the evolution of system prompts from Claude 3 in July 2024 through the latest models. Also created a git timeline tool to visualize Claude system prompt changes as commits.\",\n   275→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   276→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   277→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/18/claude-opus-4-7-system-prompt/\",\n   278→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n   279→    \"topics\": [\"AI\", \"prompt engineering\", \"Generative AI\", \"LLMs\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"AI ethics\", \"system prompts\"],\n   280→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   281→  },\n   282→  {\n   283→    \"title\": \"Agentic Engineering: Adding a new content type to blog-to-newsletter tool\",\n   284→    \"description\": \"Example of a deceptively short prompt that accomplished significant work in a single shot using AI coding tools. Simon uses AI to generate his weekly Substack newsletter from blog content, and demonstrated how Claude Code helped add new content types to his blog-to-newsletter tool.\",\n   285→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   286→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   287→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/18/blog-to-newsletter/\",\n   288→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n   289→    \"topics\": [\"AI\", \"LLMs\", \"prompt engineering\", \"coding agents\", \"AI assisted programming\", \"Generative AI\", \"agentic engineering\", \"github\"],\n   290→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   291→  },\n   292→  {\n   293→    \"title\": \"Join us at PyCon US 2026 in Long Beach—we have new AI and security tracks this year\",\n   294→    \"description\": \"PyCon US 2026 announcement taking place May 13-19 in Long Beach, California. First time on West Coast since 2017 and first time in California since 2013. Notable addition of new AI and security tracks this year.\",\n   295→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   296→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   297→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/17/pycon-2026/\",\n   298→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   299→    \"topics\": [\"conferences\", \"open-source\", \"pycon\", \"python\", \"AI\", \"psf\"],\n   300→    \"type\": \"announcement\"\n   301→  },\n   302→  {\n   303→    \"title\": \"Release: datasette-public 0.4a1 and datasette 1.0a28\",\n   304→    \"description\": \"Two Datasette releases. datasette-public 0.4a1 makes selected databases and tables visible to the public. datasette 1.0a28 addresses breakages from 1.0a27 including compatibility bug with execute_write_fn() callbacks, database.close() improvements, and new datasette.close() method. Most changes implemented using Claude Code and Claude Opus 4.7.\",\n   305→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   306→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   307→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/17/datasette-1-0a28/\",\n   308→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   309→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\"],\n   310→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   311→  },\n   312→  {\n   313→    \"title\": \"Release: llm-anthropic 0.25\",\n   314→    \"description\": \"New release adding support for claude-opus-4.7 with thinking_effort: xhigh. New thinking_display and thinking_adaptive boolean options. Increased default max_tokens to maximum allowed for each model. No longer uses obsolete structured-outputs-2025-11-13 beta header for older models.\",\n   315→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   316→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   317→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/16/llm-anthropic-0-25/\",\n   318→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   319→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\"],\n   320→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   321→  },\n   322→  {\n   323→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on my laptop drew me a better pelican than Claude Opus 4.7\",\n   324→    \"description\": \"Comparison of pelican-on-bicycle image generation between two major model releases: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B from Alibaba and Claude Opus 4.7 from Anthropic. Simon noted that for anyone taking his pelican benchmark seriously, Qwen produced better results. Discusses local LLM capabilities and LM Studio.\",\n   325→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   326→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   327→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/16/qwen-opus-pelican/\",\n   328→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   329→    \"topics\": [\"AI\", \"Generative AI\", \"local LLMs\", \"LLMs\", \"anthropic\", \"claude\", \"qwen\", \"pelican-riding-a-bicycle\", \"LLM release\", \"lm-studio\"],\n   330→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   331→  },\n   332→  {\n   333→    \"title\": \"Tool: datasette.io news preview\",\n   334→    \"description\": \"Built a custom preview UI for the datasette.io news section using Claude Artifacts. The tool allows pasting YAML content to preview rendering and highlight markdown or YAML errors. Built using standard claude.ai with Claude's ability to clone GitHub repos and examine content.\",\n   335→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   336→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   337→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/16/datasette-io-news-preview/\",\n   338→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   339→    \"topics\": [\"vibe-coding\", \"claude\", \"tools\", \"datasette\"],\n   340→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   341→  },\n   342→  {\n   343→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: Agentic Coding Power, Now Open to All\",\n   344→    \"description\": \"Alibaba open-sourced Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, a sparse yet remarkably capable mixture-of-experts (MoE) model with 35 billion total parameters and only 3 billion active parameters. Despite its efficiency, delivers outstanding agentic coding performance, surpassing Qwen3.5-35B-A3B and rivaling much larger models. Can run locally.\",\n   345→    \"author\": \"Qwen Team (Alibaba)\",\n   346→    \"source\": \"Platform\",\n   347→    \"url\": \"https://qwen.ai\",\n   348→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   349→    \"topics\": [\"qwen\", \"AI\", \"LLMs\", \"open-source\", \"agentic coding\", \"MoE\", \"local LLMs\"],\n   350→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   351→  },\n   352→  {\n   353→    \"title\": \"Release: datasette-export-database 0.3a1 and datasette 1.0a27\",\n   354→    \"description\": \"Two Datasette releases. datasette-export-database 0.3a1 upgraded to work with Datasette 1.0a27's new CSRF approach. Datasette 1.0a27 introduces two major changes: (1) No longer uses Django-style CSRF form tokens, instead using modern browser headers per Filippo Valsorda's research; (2) New RenameTableEvent fired when table is renamed during SQLite transaction.\",\n   355→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   356→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   357→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/15/datasette-1-0a27/\",\n   358→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   359→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\", \"python\"],\n   360→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   361→  },\n   362→  {\n   363→    \"title\": \"Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS\",\n   364→    \"description\": \"Google released Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, a new text-to-speech model that can be directed using prompts. Simon experimented with the model's detailed prompting guide, which includes elaborate scene descriptions, director's notes, style instructions, and sample context. Generated audio with different accents (Brixton London, Newcastle, Exeter Devon). Used Gemini 3.1 Pro to vibe code a UI for testing.\",\n   365→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   366→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   367→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/15/gemini-flash-tts/\",\n   368→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   369→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"text-to-speech\", \"tools\", \"AI\", \"prompt engineering\", \"Generative AI\", \"LLMs\", \"gemini\", \"LLM release\", \"vibe-coding\"],\n   370→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   371→  },\n   372→  {\n   373→    \"title\": \"Release: datasette-ports 0.3\",\n   374→    \"description\": \"Small update for tool that helps manage Datasette instances on laptop. New features: show working directory derived from each PID, show full path to each database file. Helps track all running Datasette instances and their database files.\",\n   375→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   376→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   377→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/15/datasette-ports-0-3/\",\n   378→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   379→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\"],\n   380→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   381→  },\n   382→  {\n   383→    \"title\": \"Zig 0.16.0 release notes: \\\"Juicy Main\\\"\",\n   384→    \"description\": \"Zig 0.16.0 introduces \\\"Juicy Main\\\" - a dependency injection feature for main() function where accepting a process.Init parameter grants access to useful properties including general purpose allocator, default I/O implementation, environment variables, and CLI arguments. Simon praised Zig's comprehensive release notes with relevant usage examples.\",\n   385→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   386→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   387→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/15/zig-0-16-0/\",\n   388→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   389→    \"topics\": [\"zig\"],\n   390→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   391→  }\n   392→]\n   393→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
